> I just started playing a monk and my blessed spell book is light blue
> and my uncursed stuff is white.  However, my spells are not colored
> like I'd hoped and when I hit "D" The option "U - Items known to be
> uncursed" is red for some reason.  How can I change this?

I can't help you with your spell menucolors without seeing your rcfile
(and what you intend to accomplish); I hope my failure colors above are
adequate. However, the latter problem is, most likely, caused by
"cursed"=red in your menucolors. "cursed" matches the word "uncursed".
The easiest fix is to include a space before the word cursed; this
makes it stop matching "uncursed" and also "!cursed". I do this for
just about all of my menucolors, so, for example, I can name a bag
"!holding" and it won't trigger the bag of holding color.

> My other question is about watching other players.  So you know, I'm
> playing using Windows XP, DECgraphics are off, IBMgraphics are on.
> Generally when I watch other players their graphics are messed up.  The
> doors look like giant ants and the walls look like mumaks and kobolds.
> Weird!  Is that because these players are not using Windows?  Because
> sometimes I watch someone and their graphics are just like mine.  What'
> s up?

It sounds like your client doesn't support DECgraphics, which is
unusual (most problems I've heard of are clients not supporting
IBMgraphics). Hit "s" a few times when watching a player and it should
strip DECgraphics down to the standard NetHack tileset.

The fix for supporting IBMgraphics is usually a change of codepage. The
fix for DECgraphics might be similarly easy, but I'm really not
familiar with such things. Are you using the builtin Windows telnet?
You shouldn't be, it's horrible. I heartily recommend using PuTTY
instead.

